<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka to aid firms in infrastructure projects.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka to aid firms in infrastructure projects.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Sri Lankan government will provide soft loans to foreign and local companies willing to invest in the country's infrastructural projects, Media Minister Dharmasiri Senanayake said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Sri Lankan cabinet has approved a plan to set up a state company to specialise in providing loans to private companies involved in infrastructure development projects, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;It is to buttress and help the development of infrastructure in Sri Lanka,&quot; Senanayake, the government spokesman, told a news conference.</p>
</text>
